 "dur": 45.043,
 "target": 45.0,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Mira hung a 600-ton golden ball inside her skyscraper.",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 3.598
  },
  {
   "text": "You see, Windport's storm winds hit 150 kilometers an hour.",
   "s": 3.798,
   "e": 7.423
  },
  {
   "text": "Her neighbor Rex laughed: \"Is that a skyscraper, or a Christmas ornament?\"",
   "s": 7.623,
   "e": 10.902
  },
  {
   "text": "Rex put a rooftop pool on his tower, and his tenants paid triple.",
   "s": 11.022,
   "e": 14.178
  },
  {
   "text": "Then came three storms. Storm one: Rex's tower swayed. Nobody noticed.",
   "s": 14.378,
   "e": 18.218
  },
  {
   "text": "Storm two: the pool sloshed and the coffee slid. But Rex grinned: \"Towers bend!\"",
   "s": 18.418,
   "e": 22.53
  },
  {
   "text": "Storm three: his tower swung two meters, and the pool waved over the edge.",
   "s": 22.65,
   "e": 25.941
  },
  {
   "text": "Then every tenant got seasick and walked out.",
   "s": 26.341,
   "e": 28.242
  },
  {
   "text": "Ever pushed a swing at the wrong moment? It stops dead.",
   "s": 28.442,
   "e": 30.862
  },
  {
   "text": "Mira's ball does that. When the tower sways one way, the ball swings the other.",
   "s": 31.062,
   "e": 34.741
  },
  {
   "text": "It pulls the tower back, so her floors barely move. Not one spilled coffee.",
   "s": 34.941,
   "e": 38.669
  },
  {
   "text": "Rex begged: \"Mira, can I borrow your ornament?\"",
   "s": 38.869,
   "e": 40.957
  },
  {
   "text": "She shrugged. Her monkey was already hanging tinsel on it.",
   "s": 41.077,
   "e": 43.743
  }
 ],
